Original replay metadata uses WORD fields and signed WORD loads.

FUN_0044ab98 writes car/mode/type/season/level/pad WORDs at 0x44aba1,
0x44abaf,0x44abbd,0x44abcb,0x44abea,0x44abfd. Its final magic WORD
store (0x44ac11) must preserve the previously written car at 0x93a492.
The replay end address at 0x93a494 remains a complete DWORD pointer.

FUN_0044ac60 reads each signed WORD using DWORD+SAR 16 at 0x44ac84
(car),0x44ac93 (mode),0x44aca8 (type),0x44acb7 (season),0x44acd2
(level),0x44ace7 (pad). Retype the fields as short to preserve both
width and sign extension. Read the car WORD directly once the magic
alias is corrected. Load_Card_File reads/compares the unsigned magic
WORD at 0x44add8; a combined magic/car DWORD prevented replay dispatch
for every nonzero saved car. Load_First_Config also stores a WORD magic.

Actual unmodified original packing/loading runs are observed with read-only
hardware breakpoints at the external LoadSave/View_Frontend_Replay call
boundaries. Native/WASM compare the packed bytes, script, car order and
load setup literally, including signed and discarded-high-half cases.
This component proof does not establish whole-game save/load or A/V parity.

